From 656616adb78fb12f315439b407a2342cbd4ba66d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gohy Yves <6154641+diogeneyves@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:00:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] cscreen: adapt the game screens to Pico board mode
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Calibration requested while no segment is known: pico_mode() (read like
  ci2c.pico_mode); calibration_needed no longer stops on empty rpi.inputs and
  rpi.outputs.
- Coin acceptor hidden: "Paramétrage" without the "Monnayeur" button (nor its
  shortcut); coins_menu refused with a message.
- "MCP" texts adapted: button LEDs subtitle "… branchées sur la carte Pico";
  banned button "Bouton … (carte Pico) banni." (banned_text).
- Buttons menu: BTN1 to BTN15 for PIN_* (and MISS for PIN_MISSDART), V1 to V12
  for LIGHT_*, T1 to T8 for TOY*; "Carte Pico absente" if the Pico is not
  there; the list of choices no longer grows on each tab change; on a swap,
  MISS does not move to another button.
- Wizard: "Carte Pico" choice always offered (warning without blocking if
  /dev/cible is missing); set_pico_card_config preset, no pins, no extension
  board, no calibration (requested at the next start). LEDs: fixed channels,
  target 0 and strip 1; target: brightness and colour order; strip: count
  (0 to 300, 0 = no strip), brightness, order. Target ring (channel 0,
  [LEDTarget]): list "Anneau 204 LED (sans pneu)" (default), "244 LED, pneu
  avant les quarts", "244 LED, pneu après", "Aucune" (set_dartcab_leds_config).
  Configuration written, then restart.
- calibrate_target: CAL 0 sent at the start (a diagnostic may have left CAL 1,
  which hwd would send back to the Pico); never CAL 1 (specification § 7.2).

Normal mode unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
